{:edb/db-before-t 2208 :edb/db-after-t 2209 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535521 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:44:23.241Z" 13194139535521 true] [17592186133835 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353502 13194139535521 true] [17592186133835 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353509 13194139535521 true] [17592186133836 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353481 13194139535521 true] [17592186133836 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353488 13194139535521 true] [17592186133836 1020 #edb/ref 17592186353495 13194139535521 true] [17592186353481 1017 #edb/ref 17592186353482 13194139535521 true] [17592186353481 1089 "q-140049" 13194139535521 true] [17592186353481 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535521 true] [17592186353481 1100 "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ is a triangular matrix\n- $A$ does not have identical rows\n- $A$ does not have proportional columns" 13194139535521 true] [17592186353481 1113 #uuid "0fee5ebf-ea7a-5f52-b051-47b6eb42b4bb" 13194139535521 true] [17592186353481 1145 "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2=5\\ne 0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ is not a triangular matrix.\n\n- Statements II and III are true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\nHence, if $|A|\\ne 0$ then $A$ doesn't have proportional nor identical rows/columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." 13194139535521 true] [17592186353482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353483 13194139535521 true] [17592186353482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353484 13194139535521 true] [17592186353482 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353485 13194139535521 true] [17592186353482 1000 #edb/ref 175921